socrates: the ABL-handoff systematic pass — no reset; attrs, NOP, REPORT LUNS, SSU, dumps

The kernel never HCE-resets a ready host: an HCE reset from the kernel
wedges the UIC command layer (flash #6: the boot's second reset; flash
#13: its FIRST), while the ABL's handoff state completes every query and
SCSI command (flashes #7-#12). The root probe takes the link over as the
ABL left it and walks the M2 playbook on that state, everything dumped
for one-photo diagnosis.

The helpers (forward-declared, then defined BEFORE the probe function
that calls them - the first CI round died on C99 use-before-declare):
READ_ATTR dump (bBootLUNEn idn 0x00, bCurrentPowerMode idn 0x01), NOP OUT
(the UFS-native link ping), REPORT LUNS (the M2 v6 lesson: the 04/02
sense is LUN-level - enumerate first), SSU POWER_CONDITION=ACTIVE (the
initializing command the sense requests), and a controller-state dump on
failure (hce/hcs/is/ucmd/arg2 + the UIC error-code registers 0x44 UECDL /
0x48 UECPA - the Linux-ufshcd diagnosis axes).
